# clang -S text and msil-ld --lto-emit-asm text without references of right declarations of every row that whole-program text checks when it runs: 'this-val' DateTime getters, 'this-obj' getters (StringBuilder::get_Length, Type::get_StructLayoutAttribute, Stream::get_CanRead of a MemoryStream before and after it is disposed), 'this-obj' members of interfaces (ICollection::get_Count of an ArrayList that ArrayList::Add filled, IDisposable::Dispose of the MemoryStream), instance fields through 'this-val' (a FILETIME's dwLowDateTime) and 'this-obj' handles (StructLayoutAttribute's CharSet, an 'enum' value), constructors of value types (DateTime's, and HandleRef's .ctor(object, native int), a delegate constructor's parameters) and of classes (StringBuilder's, ArrayList's, MemoryStream's, and FileStream's in a stub with msil_catch), 'enum' results (DateTime::get_DayOfWeek, get_Kind), an 'enum' parameter (DateTime::SpecifyKind's DateTimeKind) and two in a stub with msil_catch (FileStream's constructor on a missing file); and the rows that keep no check (a 'this-val' Int64, a 'this-obj' String, a 'this-gch' Free); the TEXT lines pin the checks in both texts, the images verify, and the program prints the same on every runtime as before the checks.
# Plan 5.20.6 MW2 as amended for MC-1 (whole-program text checks the
# declaration when it runs; text-value-type-as-reference.test,
# text-reference-type-as-value.test, text-enum-param.test and
# text-enum-result.test are the wrong declarations): the castclass of a
# 'this-obj' stub's handle, the unbox of a 'this-val' stub's object and the
# instruction after a constructor's newobj name TYPE as a TypeSpec of the
# declared kind ('castclass class [mscorlib]T' for a class or an interface,
# 'unbox valuetype [mscorlib]V'; after the newobj, 'castclass class
# [mscorlib]T' for a class and, for a value type's 'boxed' result, 'box
# valuetype [mscorlib]V' in place of the box's TypeRef), which the type
# loader accepts when the kind is right; and the stub of each 'enum'
# parameter and 'enum' result tests, at the very start of its body and
# before the .try of msil_catch, that E is an enum (typeof(E).IsEnum:
# ldtoken E, Type::GetTypeFromHandle, Type::get_IsEnum) of the C integer's
# size (sizeof E), with no local; the checks take the stub's first label
# numbers, and its other labels move up by two per check. TYPE
# System.String or System.Object as a class and a primitive value type
# (System.Int64 here) as a value type, in a 'this-obj', 'this-val' or
# constructor stub, 'this-gch', static members and the conversions' own
# castclass, unbox.any and box (a method's 'boxed' result's box among them)
# keep their TypeRef: their kinds are fixed or already in the signature. A
# constructor's TYPE is in no signature (a MemberRef's signature leaves out
# its owner's kind), hence its TypeSpec. A right declaration runs exactly
# as without the checks. The program needs no reference: the text names
# [mscorlib], which the .NET Framework and .NET (through its facade)
# resolve. At -O0 and -O2: clang -S, and clang -flto -c
# with an --lto-emit-asm link that passes no reference (%{msil_ref_flags} is
# empty whatever the leg); the TEXT lines check both texts (the stubs'
# function numbers differ, so their labels are matched as patterns); each
# text is assembled by %ilasm -exe, verified (ILVerify and, on Windows,
# PEVerify, with no new message), force-JITted (jitall) and run on the
# configured runtime and, by %{msil_also_run_check}, on each runtime of the
# leg's msil_also_run, and with msil_run_netfx on the .NET Framework 4.8;
# every transcript matches the CHECK lines. 2024-05-06 is a Monday
# (DayOfWeek 1), DateTimeKind.Utc is 1, FileStream's FileNotFoundException
# for a file that does not exist maps to its code 2, a default FILETIME's
# fields are 0, and the StructLayoutAttribute of ComTypes.FILETIME has
# CharSet Ansi (2), as conversions.test measured. No composite builds this
# test, so no equivalence oracle compares the text with an object link. Plan
# 5.17.13 (MC-1, M3/13-managed-calls).
# REDEFINE: %{msil_ref_flags} =
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && mkdir -p %t/O0 %t/O2
# DEFINE: %{tc_level} = O0
# DEFINE: %{tc_form} = text
# DEFINE: %{tc_image} = %t/%{tc_level}/%{tc_form}
# REDEFINE: %{msil_also_run_image} = %{tc_image}.exe
# DEFINE: %{tc_text} = \
# DEFINE:   FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TEXT \
# DEFINE:     --implicit-check-not="unbox [mscorlib]System.DateTime" \
# DEFINE:     --implicit-check-not="castclass [mscorlib]System.Text.StringBuilder"
# DEFINE: %{tc_build} = \
# DEFINE:   %clang_msil %{msil_cflags} -%{tc_level} -S %t/main.c -o %t/%{tc_level}/text.il \
# DEFINE:   && %{tc_text} --input-file=%t/%{tc_level}/text.il \
# DEFINE:   && %ilasm -exe -output=%t/%{tc_level}/text.exe %t/%{tc_level}/text.il \
# DEFINE:   && %clang_msil %{msil_cflags} -%{tc_level} -flto -c %t/main.c -o %t/%{tc_level}/main.o \
# DEFINE:   && %clang_msil -%{tc_level} %{msil_ldflags} -Wl,--lto-emit-asm %t/%{tc_level}/main.o -o %t/%{tc_level}/lto.il \
# DEFINE:   && %{tc_text} --input-file=%t/%{tc_level}/lto.il \
# DEFINE:   && %ilasm -exe -output=%t/%{tc_level}/lto.exe %t/%{tc_level}/lto.il
# DEFINE: %{tc_run} = \
# DEFINE:   %msil_verify %{tc_image}.exe \
# DEFINE:   %if msil-jitall %{ && %msil_jitall %{tc_image}.exe %} \
# DEFINE:   && %msil_exec --out %{tc_image}.out %{tc_image}.exe \
# DEFINE:   && FileCheck --input-file=%{tc_image}.out --match-full-lines %s \
# DEFINE:   %{msil_also_run_check}
# DEFINE: %{tc_netfx} = \
# DEFINE:   %msil_exec --netfx %{msil_netfx_skip} --out %{tc_image}.netfx.out %{tc_image}.exe \
# DEFINE:   && FileCheck --input-file=%{tc_image}.netfx.out --match-full-lines %s
# RUN: %{tc_build}
# RUN: %{tc_run}
# RUN: %if msil-run-netfx %{ %{tc_netfx} %}
# REDEFINE: %{tc_form} = lto
# RUN: %{tc_run}
# RUN: %if msil-run-netfx %{ %{tc_netfx} %}
# REDEFINE: %{tc_level} = O2
# REDEFINE: %{tc_form} = text
# RUN: %{tc_build}
# RUN: %{tc_run}
# RUN: %if msil-run-netfx %{ %{tc_netfx} %}
# REDEFINE: %{tc_form} = lto
# RUN: %{tc_run}
# RUN: %if msil-run-netfx %{ %{tc_netfx} %}
# The checks in both texts, stub by stub in the order the texts print them.
# A value type's constructor: the box of its 'boxed' result names DateTime
# as a value type.
# TEXT-LABEL: .method assembly static native int '__msil_mc.new_date'(int32, int32, int32) cil managed
# TEXT:       newobj instance void [mscorlib]System.DateTime::.ctor(int32, int32, int32)
