# Classes' constructors without parameters, and 'this-obj' members of
# interfaces: a castclass right after ArrayList's and MemoryStream's newobj
# names them as classes, and the castclass of the 'this' handle names
# ICollection and IDisposable as a class too (the TypeSpec's 'class' stands
# for every reference type); the interface stubs have no local.
# TEXT-LABEL: .method assembly static native int '__msil_mc.new_list'() cil managed
# TEXT:       newobj instance void [mscorlib]System.Collections.ArrayList::.ctor()
# TEXT-NEXT:  castclass class [mscorlib]System.Collections.ArrayList
# TEXT-NEXT:  dup
# TEXT-LABEL: .method assembly static int32 '__msil_mc.collection_count'(native int) cil managed
# TEXT-NOT:   .locals
# TEXT:       castclass class [mscorlib]System.Collections.ICollection
# TEXT-NEXT:  @MC{{[0-9]+}}_1:
# TEXT-NEXT:  callvirt instance int32 [mscorlib]System.Collections.ICollection::get_Count()
# TEXT-LABEL: .method assembly static native int '__msil_mc.new_stream'() cil managed
# TEXT:       newobj instance void [mscorlib]System.IO.MemoryStream::.ctor()
# TEXT-NEXT:  castclass class [mscorlib]System.IO.MemoryStream
